# Directory patterns that a module or feature name could match (logs, tmp,
# build, ...) are anchored to where tools write them: the repository root and
# the package roots (apps/*, packages/*). Unanchored, `logs/` would also hide
# apps/api/app/modules/logs/ from `pnpm new:module logs`, which refuses names
# git would ignore. Secret directories are the exception: they are ignored at
# every depth, so `pnpm new:module secrets` is refused.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and environment files — never commit real values.
# Only the placeholder template is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env*` also catches sync-conflict and editor copies such as `.env 2` or
# `.env~`, and `.envrc`.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.jks
*.keystore
.secrets/
secrets/
.vercel/.env*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / TypeScript
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.npm/
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.next/
/out/
/*/*/out/
/dist/
/*/*/dist/
/build/
/*/*/build/
.turbo/
.vite/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

